{
 "spec": 3,
 "what": "The one list, read by the site (js/words.js) and by the robot (tools/words.py). It is a guard, not moderation: it stops SIXFINGERS printing a racist word or a call to hatred in its own chrome or under its own robot's name. It is not a profanity filter, and ordinary swearing is deliberately let through.",
 "rule": [
  "A word enters only if it is unambiguously a racist insult, a call to hatred, or a nazi slogan. Not rude, not coarse, nothing merely sexual.",
  "It must not be a surname, a first name, a place or a demonym. If it is also an ordinary word it may still enter, but only with match: word, and the known collision is written in its note.",
  "match: anywhere needs at least five letters. Below that a run of letters turns up inside too many ordinary words.",
  "Missing things is the intended setting. A guard that refuses somebody's real name does far more harm than a word that gets through on a page nobody else reads.",
  "An entry written with spaces is a SLOGAN, and it is matched against whole words in a row. That is what keeps race warmup and wholesale racing out of it, while race war and r a c e w a r are still caught.",
  "When an entry is kept although it collides with something ordinary, the collision is written down in known_collisions. A trade that is written down can be reversed by deleting one line; a trade that is silent cannot.",
  "An entry that collides with something ordinary goes to the review tier instead of being dropped. Refusing an innocent person is the expensive mistake; holding their proposal for a minute is not."
 ],
 "kept_out": {
  "nigga": "widely reclaimed, and refusing it would refuse ordinary speech (rule 1)",
  "kike": "four letters, and Kike is a common Spanish diminutive carried by living people (rules 2 and 3)",
  "negre": "an insult, and a real French surname (rule 2)",
  "negro": "the ordinary word for the colour black in Spanish and Portuguese (rule 2)",
  "bamboula": "used as a racist insult in France, and also a Caribbean drum and dance (rule 2)",
  "retard": "the ordinary French word for lateness (rule 2)",
  "dyke": "a wall against the sea, and the surname Van Dyke (rule 2)",
  "yid": "reclaimed by a football crowd, and three letters (rules 1 and 3)",
  "zyd": "the ordinary Polish word for a Jewish person. Only the Cyrillic form is refused",
  "macaco": "the ordinary Portuguese word for monkey (rule 2)",
  "fag": "British slang for a cigarette (rule 2)",
  "sale race": "the French phrase is a real insult, but as a run of letters it also sits inside wholesale racecar. Dropped rather than accepted, because a false refusal is the expensive kind of mistake"
 },
